  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Fig. 6, 'Planning and implementing a digital health enterprise: phases, steps and resources'. Seven numbered phases run down the left: 01 Assessing the current state and enabling environment; 02 Establishing a shared understanding and strategic planning; 03 Defining the future state; 04 Planning the enterprise architecture; 05 Determining health content requirements; 06 M&E of digital health implementations and fostering data use; 07 Implementing, maintaining and scaling. Each phase lists its steps, for example 'Develop a national digital health strategy' in phase 02 and 'Identify validated health content appropriate for the implementation context' in phase 05. To the right, resource tiles are placed against the phase(s) they serve, some spanning several phases, and each is marked as a PDF for print or an online environment. They include the WHO–ITU national eHealth strategy toolkit, the Digital implementation investment guide (DIIG), the WHO SMART guidelines with digital adaptation kits and machine-readable recommendations, TOGAF, Open HIE, ICD-11, HL7 FHIR, LOINC, the WHO MAPS toolkit and Ethics and governance of artificial intelligence for health. The tile 'WHO handbook for digitalizing primary health care (this document)' sits in phase 05.",
